# GeoSAM2 — configuration template
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# The .env file is NOT committed to git (.gitignore).
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.dist .env
#   # edit .env
#   python app.py             # step-by-step app  -> http://127.0.0.1:7862
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── API keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Only the VLM stage (seed view, describe, part map) needs keys: one per provider named in the
# GEOSAM2_*_MODEL chains below. With the defaults, GEMINI_API_KEY alone is required.
# Get yours at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=


# ── VLM ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The models behind the seed: one picks the view and describes the object, one paints its part map.
# Each is a chain of pydantic-ai 'provider:model' names, comma-separated, tried in order: the first
# whose key is set answers, the later ones take over when it fails (quota, outage, refused key).
# A link whose key is unset is skipped. Any provider pydantic-ai knows is a valid link, a gateway
# included: e.g. keep Claude on its own key and let OpenRouter back Gemini with
#   GEOSAM2_DESCRIBE_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6,openrouter:google/gemini-3.7-flash
#   GEOSAM2_PAINT_MODEL=openrouter:google/gemini-3.1-flash-image
# GEOSAM2_DESCRIBE_MODEL=google:gemini-3.7-flash,google:gemini-3.8-flash,google:gemini-3.1-pro-preview
# GEOSAM2_PAINT_MODEL=google:gemini-3.1-flash-image,google:gemini-2.5-flash-image


# ── Development ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Log level. DEBUG adds the per-part pixel coverage of a generated mask.
# GEOSAM2_LOG_LEVEL=INFO


# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Host and port for app.py (uncomment to override the defaults shown).
# GEOSAM2_APP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# GEOSAM2_APP_PORT=7862
